# Public build-time values only.
#
# Everything with a VITE_ prefix is inlined into the browser bundle, so
# treat this file as published to the world. Secrets — AUTH_SECRET,
# MSG91_AUTH_KEY, POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN, OPENAI_API_KEY, any Google client
# secret — belong in backend/.env and must never appear here.
#
# These are read at build time, so restart `npm run dev` after editing.

# Leave empty for same-origin: the Vite dev proxy (and nginx in production)
# relays /api to the backend, keeping the session cookie first-party. Set a
# URL only to bypass the proxy and talk to a remote API directly.
VITE_API_URL=

# The Client ID from Google Cloud Console → Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client IDs
# (not the Client Secret, which this sign-in flow never uses). The same value
# goes in backend/.env as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID: the browser uses it to render
# Google's button, the API uses it as the audience a token must be minted for,
# and a mismatch between the two fails verification.
#
# Leaving it empty hides Google sign-in; phone and email codes still work.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
